\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Qualitative comparison} on test views (crops of the boxed region; PSNR of the full view), each at the median of LiSA\xspace  's per-view margin over the best baseline in its scene. Rows: the two GS$^3$\xspace  scenes dominated by cast shadows, a real capture on which the methods are close, and the synthetic scene where we trail most. Per-primitive shadows of SSD-GS and GS$^3$\xspace  fragment the moving shadows of the vase handle and the hot dogs, which pixel receivers reading the atlas reproduce; LiSA\xspace  misses the thin streak on the Drums cymbal. More scenes, including Fish, are in the supplement.}}{7}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:comparison}{{3}{7}{\textbf {Qualitative comparison} on test views (crops of the boxed region; PSNR of the full view), each at the median of \ours 's per-view margin over the best baseline in its scene. Rows: the two \gsthree scenes dominated by cast shadows, a real capture on which the methods are close, and the synthetic scene where we trail most. Per-primitive shadows of SSD-GS and \gsthree fragment the moving shadows of the vase handle and the hot dogs, which pixel receivers reading the atlas reproduce; \ours misses the thin streak on the Drums cymbal. More scenes, including Fish, are in the supplement}{figure.caption.17}{}}
